# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cold Email Agent – Cloud Functions Secrets Reference
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloud Functions use Firebase Secret Manager, NOT .env files.
# This file documents all required secrets so new contributors know
# what to provision. It is safe to commit.
#
# To set each secret, run:
#   firebase functions:secrets:set SECRET_NAME
# Then enter the value when prompted.
#
# To use secrets locally with the emulator, create
# functions/.secret.local (already git-ignored) with the format below.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Required Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# ENCRYPTION_SALT
#   Purpose : Salt used in PBKDF2 key derivation for AES-GCM encryption
#             of SMTP passwords. Must match VITE_ENCRYPTION_SALT in the
#             frontend .env.local.
#   Set via : firebase functions:secrets:set ENCRYPTION_SALT
#   Local   : Add to functions/.secret.local (see below)
#
# ENCRYPTION_SALT=change_me_to_a_long_random_string

# ── Local Emulator (.secret.local) ────────────────────────────────
# Create functions/.secret.local for local emulator use:
#
#   ENCRYPTION_SALT=same_value_as_VITE_ENCRYPTION_SALT_in_frontend_env_local
#
# functions/.secret.local is already in .gitignore — never commit it.
